WEBVTT

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:13.080
I've always been bad at playing.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.660
Come on, give me your hand!

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.440
Wait for me!

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:21.360
I couldn't figure out what I find to be fun.

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.330
So, maybe, I was just waiting for this.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:26.830
Miki.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.160
Miki-chan!

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:36.550
Yes, waiting to meet someone
who can help me find what fun is.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:41.510
And that became a reality.

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:53.270
I met Aya-chan at Kamogawa River.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:59.250
Then I was introduced to
analog games on the same day

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.490
by Midori-chan at the
Saikoro Club, with the manager.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:02.610
So...

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:06.160
We beat him!

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:13.540
Then we met Emmy, and we dressed up
as maids to run a board game café.

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:17.460
Miki-chan.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:20.800
You're early, Miki-chan.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.200
Did you wait long?

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.160
No.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.760
Okay, let's go to school.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:25.760
Okay.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:04.040
Live a regular life to make sure
you are all healthy

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:03.190
Today is the last day of
our first year in high school...

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:06.030
when you return next semester.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:09.200
That is the end of my talk.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:13.160
Goodbye, first-year student me!

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:11.530
All bow!

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:16.370
Come on, second-year student me!

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:18.040
What does that even mean?

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:20.580
Oh, well.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:25.250
But really, the year flew by instantly.

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:26.550
Yeah...

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:30.850
I transferred midyear,
so it was even shorter for me.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.700
What's up, Miki?

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:36.540
Hmm?

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.350
You looked really happy.

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:41.560
Oh... yeah.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:47.280
I was just thinking back
on how fun this year was.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:50.780
More than any other year...

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.240
Miki...

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:55.620
I'm also glad I was able to--

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:56.450
Yes!

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:59.620
I'm so happy I was able to meet you, Miki!

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:00.630
Emmy...!

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.500
She beat me to it...!

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:06.330
I'm glad to have met you, too, Miki-chan!

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:08.470
Thank you, Aya-chan.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:15.330
If only these fun times could last forever...

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:15.330
Oh, we share the same opinion, Aya!

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:16.640
But of course!

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:23.110
Hey, next school year, wouldn't it
be cool if Emmy was in the same class?

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:26.110
What are you talking about, Aya?
That's not possible.

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:28.080
Huh? Why?

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:32.070
Starting in the second year,
the classes separate by major.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:36.250
Emmy and I are going into the sciences.
You and Miki are in humanities.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:36.910
Huh?

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:38.080
Wait, what?

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:42.500
So at least two of us are
going to be separated...

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:45.040
...or we could end up all separated!

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:47.000
Seriously?

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:51.300
Hey, in that case, can we at least go on
a trip together during spring break?

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.500
Sounds good!

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:53.430
Nice!

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.890
Yay!

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:57.040
I'm so sorry, Aya.

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:58.160
Huh?

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:00.730
I'm spending spring break in Germany.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:04.480
I haven't seen my grandmother
in Germany for a long time now.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:08.280
My parents and I are going to see her.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.500
I see...

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:13.160
That's very important.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:18.040
I'm sure your grandmother
will be happy to see you back.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.450
Yes, thank you, Miki.

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:26.040
There's also one other reason
I want to go back to Germany.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:26.710
Huh?

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:30.380
My dad knows an editor at a game publisher.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:33.130
I want to show him my game.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:37.410
In Germany, if you want
to become a game author,

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:41.270
you bring your game
to an editor to show them.

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:47.080
If they like what they see,
it's not unlikely for them to publish it.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.450
I see...

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:51.120
Wait, you made a game, Emmy?

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:56.750
Yes! I was moved by how Midori
submitted her game to the competition!

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:57.740
By me?

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:02.540
I thought I should work hard
to realize my dream, too!

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:04.120
Emmy...

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:08.160
Actually... the results for
that competition already arrived.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:08.880
Huh?!

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:12.380
Seriously?! So how was it? Can I look?

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:13.510
Yeah...

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:20.200
"Dear new game designer,

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:23.520
first of all, thank you for applying
to our company's competition"...

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:27.980
We all had a lot of fun playing your game.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:32.620
The way you designed the board to allow
free collection and arrangement of furniture

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:34.070
was truly outstanding.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:37.530
Several of the members of my team
rated your game quite highly.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:40.120
Quite highly! Wow!

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.120
That's great.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:43.200
Read it till the end...

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:46.330
"But"...

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:50.130
...I still felt that there were
some pieces missing.

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:55.840
I especially felt the mechanics
of the game needed improvement.

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:59.800
Due to this, I unfortunately must
inform you that your game has failed.

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:05.120
But please don't be disappointed.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:13.540
If you are serious about becoming a
game designer, you can and must improve.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:14.940
This is my way of encouraging
and supporting you.

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:20.830
If you have the desire to improve further,
I recommend that you visit us here.

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:29.540
Coming to see how games are really made
should be an invaluable experience for you.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:32.000
..."to this invitation, but think about it.

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:35.950
I have high hopes for your
growth and your next game.

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:37.470
George Beresford."

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:41.080
Oh... so you didn't make the cut.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:43.680
But he said don't be disappointed...

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:46.770
And he said you should go to America.
What are you going to do, Midori-chan?!

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:49.600
America...

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:55.250
I generally prefer Euro-style
game designs, but...

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:57.450
That's what's bothering you...?

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:03.660
Emmy, are you going back
to Germany after graduation?

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:04.740
Oh...

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:11.460
I haven't decided yet. My dad says
he'll stay in Japan for a while...

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:16.970
But if I'm going to make games, living in
Germany is convenient in a lot of ways.

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:18.220
You're right.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:24.850
George's company, Bad Dwarf,
does make Euro-style games, too.

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:29.520
I'm seriously considering this offer.

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:37.410
I'm really impressed,
Midori-chan and Emmy...

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:39.280
Yeah.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:43.990
They both have things they want to do
and are working to pursue them.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:50.460
Hey, walking by Kamogawa River
together reminds us of last year, right?

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:53.500
Yeah, you really startled me.

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:55.880
You fell into the river, bicycle and all...

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:58.840
Me, too! I thought I was going to die!

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:03.300
I'm relieved... Aya-chan is still the same.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:05.120
Um...

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:05.810
Hmm?

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:09.000
Aya-chan, do you have
a thing you want to do?

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.450
Yes, of course!

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:11.270
Huh?

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:15.900
My dream is to live where
there are lots of animals!

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:20.540
Then I want to be an
animal photographer like my dad.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:25.070
Or become a veterinarian and cure
lots of animals, or something like that!

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:26.910
Or, maybe--

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:30.580
Aya-chan, if you want to become a vet,
don't you need to major in sciences?

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:35.590
Oh, right! But my point is,
there are so many things I want to do!

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:38.580
Living in South America sounds cool, too!

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:40.040
Huh? South America...

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:42.550
Hmm? What's wrong, Miki-chan?

00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:47.010
Nothing. I just thought,
it's like you always are.

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:48.470
Really?

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:02.690
They all have things they want to do...

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:05.530
Midori-chan and Emmy...

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:07.450
Aya-chan, too...

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:13.460
Is it just me? Am I the only one
who wants to stay this way?

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:27.890
Hey, Aya-chan--

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:29.510
Connecting to voicemail service.

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:31.270
Please leave a message after the tone--

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:33.060
Oh...

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:44.530
Hello...

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:47.490
Hello-- Oh, you are...

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:51.450
I'm sorry, Emmy is out shopping right now.

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:55.870
She should be back in an hour or so.
Would you like to wait here?

00:10:55.870 --> 00:11:00.580
Oh, no. Thank you!
It wasn't anything urgent. I'll come back.

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:01.590
Thank you...

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:13.500
Sorry to make you join me
for game shopping, Shibusawa.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:17.650
It's fine, as long as you're serious
about buying me that cake later.

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:20.250
Sure, count on it!

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:25.370
I might not look it, but I eat quite a lot.

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:27.570
Fine, I'll match that.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:31.830
Hey, welcome.

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:33.700
Alone? That's different.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:35.910
Um...

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:39.130
Midori-chan isn't working today.

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:44.670
Midori-chan isn't around, either...

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:48.910
What's wrong, Miki-chan? You look pale.

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:52.410
Oh, no, it's nothing.

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:53.720
Sorry to bother you...

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:56.270
Uh, Miki-chan...

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:57.940
Huh?!

00:11:59.080 --> 00:11:59.900
This one...

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:21.660
Hey, it's me. I'm downstairs.

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:23.340
The weather's nice today.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:26.160
I'll be right down, wait up!

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:28.300
Yeah, no rush.

00:12:29.620 --> 00:12:32.220
Morning, Hana. Where's breakfast?

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:34.760
It's already midday, Aya.

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:39.200
Come on, I'm on spring break.

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:42.190
Always such a child...

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:42.190
Oh.

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:43.940
It's from Miki-chan...

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:48.740
Hmm?

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:51.820
Manager?

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:54.240
Yes, this is Ono.

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:56.410
Hey, Midori-chan.

00:12:56.410 --> 00:12:59.450
Hmm? Miki was here?

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:00.160
Yeah.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:02.460
I wonder what happened...

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:09.090
Ryuji, we have to hurry!
The movie is starting soon!

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:12.470
Whose fault is this?
You're the one who was late!

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:17.200
Besides, why am I going to the
movies with you on such a nice day...

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:17.680
Hmm?

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:19.640
Huh?

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:22.790
Hey, what's up?

00:13:22.790 --> 00:13:23.690
Oh...

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:26.000
Is that Takekasa?

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:29.610
Yeah, and she looks kind of sad.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:35.200
I bought it...

00:13:36.950 --> 00:13:41.910
It looks kind of like the stuffed doll
my dad bought a long time ago...

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:45.540
Wow, so fluffy!

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:48.050
Your name is Mojarin!

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:51.170
Here you are!

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:55.640
I was so happy, I gave him a name,
which made me feel like he was alive.

00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:57.510
I used to talk to him a lot...

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:03.850
What a silly face...

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:07.400
This one is... just a baby.

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:11.530
This one is a trickster, full of energy.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:13.990
This one is spoiled.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.530
And this one is...

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:19.950
...introverted and shy.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:22.660
Just like me...

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:31.620
She won't pick up!

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:33.910
Where could she be?

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:35.300
I'm worried.

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:38.450
Oh, she's calling!

00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:39.180
Huh?

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:46.270
Hello, all! Going out together?

00:14:46.270 --> 00:14:48.830
Yes, we're going on a picnic.

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:51.700
I can't wait to unpack my lunch!

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:54.030
You eat too much!

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:56.910
Do you want to join us?

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:59.700
Are you sure?! I'm so glad!

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:04.250
Of course! I made too much lunch!

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.710
Wow, that sounds great!

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:09.920
What? Not fair! I want to go, too!

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:13.260
Of course! Let's all go together!

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:15.340
Yay! Thank you!

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:16.550
Hmm?

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:20.760
You there! Do you want to come, too?

00:15:20.970 --> 00:15:22.910
Oh, don't mind that one.

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:24.600
Huh? Why?

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:27.480
That one doesn't want to go anywhere.

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:32.580
Come on, let's go! It's a bit far,
but I know a hill with a great view.

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:34.410
Let's go! I can't wait!

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:36.040
Let's go!

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:38.080
Yes, let's go!

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:40.990
Wait... please... don't go.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:47.000
I want to stay here forever.
I want to stay here with everyone...

00:15:47.450 --> 00:15:49.580
So please stay here...

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:52.880
Stay here with me...

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:56.010
I understand.

00:15:56.750 --> 00:16:00.840
I'm too weak. I'm afraid to move forward.

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:06.290
But this is the first time
I've found something I find to be fun.

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:09.730
Is it so wrong to want to stay here?

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:12.910
Come on, now.

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:13.690
Huh?

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:19.280
That's a bad habit of yours--
always letting your thoughts turn negative.

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:22.120
Mojarin...

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:26.870
They're your friends, right?
You like them, right?

00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:33.250
Yes... I love them.

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:39.750
Then it's fine! I'm sure they
think of you the same way.

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:40.870
Hey!

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:40.870
See?

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:41.540
Huh?

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:43.180
Miki-chan!

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:45.470
Miki!

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:46.680
Everyone!

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:48.870
We were looking for you, Miki-chan!

00:16:48.870 --> 00:16:50.140
How did you know I was here?

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:52.830
Tanoue-kun called!

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:53.860
Tanoue-kun?

00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:59.080
I didn't notice you called me
last night, so I called back,

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.000
but you didn't pick up, so...

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:03.490
Huh? Oh, I didn't notice...

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:06.990
Oh, no, battery's dead...

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:12.000
The manager called me and
told me Miki was behaving strangely.

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:15.840
When I got home,
my dad told me you came by.

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:20.120
So we called you, but you didn't pick up,
so we were worried something was wrong.

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:22.450
We were looking for you.

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:24.470
Looking... for me?

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:30.730
Wh-What's wrong, Miki-chan?!

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:35.750
Sorry, I... I'm such a weakling.

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:38.860
I had so much fun this past year...

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:47.080
So us getting split up next year, and you
all having plans and moving forward...

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:51.910
But I want things to be the same...

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:55.370
I want the four of us to be together...

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:57.210
That's all I could think about... so...

00:17:57.950 --> 00:17:59.300
Miki...

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:02.370
If you all aren't around, I...

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:05.000
Miki-chan, I'm the same.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:05.760
Huh?

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:07.510
Aya-chan?

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:12.620
When I had that fight with
my dad and ran out of the house...

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:14.600
...you saved me, Miki-chan!

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:18.040
Same with me!

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:21.490
Thanks to Miki,
I was able to get close to Midori!

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:27.580
I was able to put away my
silly pride and be honest with myself.

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:30.790
Midori-chan... Emmy...

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:36.870
Miki, you're indispensable to us now.

00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:40.200
Even if we are in separate classes,
and go different places,

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:42.450
no matter how many years pass,
we'll always be friends!

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:45.470
All together! Miki, you're not alone!

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:49.430
Yes... Thank you, everyone...

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:51.640
Hmm?

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:54.810
Hey, that's <i>Toddles Bobbles</i>.
Did you just buy it?

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:57.450
Yes, just now, at the Saikoro Club.

00:18:57.450 --> 00:19:02.870
I know this one. A Russian game, where
you give weird creatures some names, right?

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:05.530
What is that?! Sounds awesome! Let's play!

00:19:05.530 --> 00:19:08.280
Sounds good. Let's play!

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:09.200
Yes!

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:10.410
Yay!

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:14.710
So, here are the rules.

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:18.170
First, shuffle the cards and make a deck.

00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:24.080
On your turn, flip a card from the top,
so, for example, "Bob!"

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:27.300
Give a name to the creature on the card.

00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:33.620
Repeat this, and when you see
a card someone already named...

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:31.000
Long-legs.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:33.620
Pinky.

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:34.350
Bob!

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:36.410
...you call out its name.

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:40.750
The person who said the name
fastest gets all of the cards.

00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:42.020
Got it!

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:45.660
The person who collects the most cards wins.

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:47.740
Sounds like fun!

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:49.620
Okay, you start, Aya.

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:50.660
Okay!

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:54.700
Hmm... Mamekichi!

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:56.750
I'll go next.

00:19:57.660 --> 00:19:58.830
Madame Curl!

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:00.790
My turn.

00:20:01.580 --> 00:20:03.500
Griessing Nars!

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:05.450
Gr... Gree...?

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:07.970
German names, huh...?
This might get tough...

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:10.220
Oh...

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:11.550
Mojarin...

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:14.140
Me again!

00:20:14.620 --> 00:20:18.350
Another new one! So cute! How about...

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:19.410
Mon-chan!

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:21.450
What kind of name is that?

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:23.700
It's the name of a pet
flying squirrel I had before!

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:25.910
You had a flying squirrel for a pet?

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:26.910
Yes!

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:28.570
Um... okay.

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:30.120
Mojarin!

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:31.030
Huh?!

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:32.280
Oh...

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:34.910
Miki-chan, so fast!

00:20:34.910 --> 00:20:37.000
Oh, Mojarin!

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:45.250
See, I told you, right?

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:48.130
Yes. Thank you, Mojarin.

00:20:49.410 --> 00:20:52.200
This is fun! Let's keep going!

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:53.760
I won't lose!

00:20:53.760 --> 00:20:55.970
Here we go!

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:10.150
Eighteen, nineteen, twenty... twenty-one.

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:12.040
Miki is in first place!

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:14.620
Wow, you're too strong, Miki-chan!

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:20.160
Even if we're in separate classes,
we'll still have our games!

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:23.080
We can play after school like this.

00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:25.540
Emmy...

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:29.760
Hey, let's make a club! A club just for us!

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:30.580
Huh...?

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:33.080
Sounds good. What should we name it?

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:36.250
Um, Analog Game Group?

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:38.040
Denied, too bland.

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:39.310
Dice Club...

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:43.410
How about After School Dice Club?

00:21:43.410 --> 00:21:46.060
We'll borrow the name of the shop.

00:21:46.370 --> 00:21:49.040
After School... Dice Club.

00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:51.790
I like it. I think the manager would, too.

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:53.200
Yay! I agree!

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:58.370
Well, that makes all of us official members
of the After School Dice Club!

00:21:58.500 --> 00:21:59.120
Yes.

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:02.000
I'll be okay.

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:05.580
I love Miki. She's kind,
unlike certain other people!

00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:08.290
I'm not who I used to be. I can move on...

00:22:05.580 --> 00:22:06.960
Hey, Aya!

00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:14.720
...because I now have friends
who can find fun with me.
